<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms pass on 23,000T wheat tenders.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms pass on 23,000T wheat tenders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd on Friday passed on tenders for 23,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat due to high offer prices, company officials said.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang invited tenders for 9,500 tonnes at basis prices over July futures on the U.S grain futures exchanges including the Chicago Board of Trade, they said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour invited the remaining 13,500 tonnes at flat prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for May 5-June 5 to the south western port of Pusan.</p>
<p>Traders said the lowest bids were made by Japanese trading house Kanematsu Corp.  </p>
<p>Details for the tenders as follows :</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		4,900   $162.05</p>
<p>(ordinally)</p>
<p>  Club wheat		1,000   $162.40</p>
<p>(min 15%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,900   $186.55</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,700   $193.35</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,400   $0.43 (over CBOT's July)</p>
<p>(ordinary)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  800   $0.43 (over CBOT's July)</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 2,500   $1.0575 (over KCBT's July)</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  2,800   $1.1725 (over MGE's July)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
